From: operator <operator@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: hda: flush posted writes after azx_int_clear()

snd_hdac_bus_init_chip() issues azx_int_clear() (one SD_STS write per
stream plus STATESTS, RIRBSTS and INTSTS) immediately followed by
snd_hdac_bus_init_cmd_io()'s CORB base/size/WP/RP writes, i.e. up to
18 back-to-back posted MMIO writes before the first read (the CORBRP
poll in azx_clear_corbrp()).

The Creative Sound Blaster AE-9 (CTHDA 1102:0010 rev 01, behind the
card's ASMedia ASM1083 PCIe-to-PCI bridge) cannot absorb that burst:
after it, every MMIO read of the controller and even config reads of
the bridge return all-ones after a ~220 ms completion timeout until the
link is reset. Because azx_clear_corbrp() then polls 1000 times under
spin_lock_irq, the probe stalls for minutes with interrupts disabled,
hard-locking the machine and taking down devices that share the
upstream switch.

Bisected with an out-of-tree replay of the exact sequence: the same
block passes, with every other variable held (stock timing, values,
IRQs off, WC ring memory, byte-wide GCTL access, bus mastering), as
soon as a single read is placed between the int-clear writes and the
CORB writes.

Read INTSTS back at the end of azx_int_clear() so the posted writes
are flushed before the command ring is programmed. This is one extra
MMIO read at init and is harmless on every other controller.

Signed-off-by: operator <operator@localhost>
---
 sound/hda/core/controller.c | 5 +++++
 sound/hda/core/stream.c     | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/sound/hda/core/controller.c
+++ b/sound/hda/core/controller.c
@@ -86,6 +86,8 @@
 		snd_hdac_chip_writeb(bus, RIRBCTL, AZX_RBCTL_DMA_EN | AZX_RBCTL_IRQ_EN);
 	/* Accept unsolicited responses */
 	snd_hdac_chip_updatel(bus, GCTL, AZX_GCTL_UNSOL, AZX_GCTL_UNSOL);
+	/* flush the CORB/RIRB setup writes before anything else touches the ring */
+	snd_hdac_chip_readl(bus, GCTL);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(snd_hdac_bus_init_cmd_io);
 
@@ -599,6 +601,9 @@
 
 	/* clear int status */
 	snd_hdac_chip_writel(bus, INTSTS, AZX_INT_CTRL_EN | AZX_INT_ALL_STREAM);
+
+	/* flush the burst of posted writes before touching the CORB/RIRB */
+	snd_hdac_chip_readl(bus, INTSTS);
 }
 
 /**
--- a/sound/hda/core/stream.c
+++ b/sound/hda/core/stream.c
@@ -292,6 +292,8 @@
 	/* upper BDL address */
 	snd_hdac_stream_writel(azx_dev, SD_BDLPU,
 			       upper_32_bits(azx_dev->bdl.addr + bus->addr_offset));
+	/* flush the burst of posted writes (see azx_int_clear) */
+	snd_hdac_stream_readl(azx_dev, SD_BDLPU);
 
 	/* enable the position buffer */
 	if (bus->use_posbuf && bus->posbuf.addr) {
@@ -341,6 +343,8 @@
 	snd_hdac_stream_writel(azx_dev, SD_BDLPL, 0);
 	snd_hdac_stream_writel(azx_dev, SD_BDLPU, 0);
 	snd_hdac_stream_writel(azx_dev, SD_CTL, 0);
+	/* flush the burst of posted writes (see azx_int_clear) */
+	snd_hdac_stream_readl(azx_dev, SD_CTL);
 	azx_dev->bufsize = 0;
 	azx_dev->period_bytes = 0;
 	azx_dev->format_val = 0;
